On Friday 01 May 2009 06:08:11 tijlan wrote:
> Is it possible to prefix a fu'ivla with more than one rafsi? For example:
>
>  zgikle-r-jazu (the genre of Jazz music)
>  zgitadj-r-jazu (the techniques of Jazz music)
>
> mu'o se ckire spuda mi'e tijlan

Allowing type-3 fu'ivla to have two prefixes has been found unworkable. It is 
possible (though not official), though, to use a type-3 fu'ivla to make a 
lujvo, such as "zgikrjazytadji".

Btw, "zgike" doesn't have a CVC rafsi, and "zik" is unallocated. Why?

